# 23. Voting Classifier

A Voting Classifier combines predictions from multiple base classifiers.

The paper uses:

```text
SVM + LGBM + Extra Trees
```

for its soft voting classifier.

In soft voting, the predicted probabilities from the base models are combined and the class with the highest combined probability is selected.

---

# 24. Stacking Classifier

The Stacking Classifier is the most important model in this paper.

It combines multiple base models and uses another model as a meta-classifier.

The paper uses:

```text
SVM
   +
Extra Trees
   +
LGBM
   ↓
Stacking Classifier
```

The base models generate predictions.

These predictions are then provided to the meta-classifier, which learns how to combine them to produce the final classification.

This allows the final model to take advantage of the strengths of different classifiers.

---

# 25. Why Stacking is Important in This Paper

The authors report that the Stacking Classifier achieves the strongest overall performance among the evaluated ML models.

The paper attributes this to its ability to combine predictions from multiple models.

For example:

* SVM may capture certain decision boundaries,
* Extra Trees may capture nonlinear relationships,
* LGBM may capture powerful tree-based patterns.

The stacking mechanism learns how to combine their outputs.

Therefore, instead of asking:

> Which single model is best?

the approach asks:

> How can the predictions of multiple strong models be combined?

This is highly relevant to our project because our project also focuses on **optimized explainable ensemble learning**.

