# 32. Evaluation Metrics

The paper uses several metrics.

## Accuracy

Measures the proportion of correctly classified samples.

```text
Accuracy =
Correct Predictions / Total Predictions
```

---

## Precision

Measures how many predicted positive cases are actually positive.

```text
Precision =
TP / (TP + FP)
```

---

## Recall

Measures how many actual positive cases are correctly identified.

```text
Recall =
TP / (TP + FN)
```

---

## F1-score

Combines precision and recall.

```text
F1 =
2 × Precision × Recall
/
(Precision + Recall)
```

---

## ROC-AUC

Measures the model's ability to distinguish between classes across classification thresholds.

The paper reports a final ROC-AUC of:

**99.8%**

for the proposed stacking classifier.

---

## Learning Curve

Learning curves are used to investigate model behavior as the amount of training data increases.

They can help identify:

* underfitting,
* overfitting,
* generalization behavior.

